<h1><%= @sheet.name %></h1>
<p class="muted">
  sheet <code><%= @sheet.slug %></code> · created <%= @sheet.created_at %> ·
  saved <%= @sheet.updated_at %>
</p>

<%= render "form", persisted: true %>

<h2>Start</h2>
<div class="card">
  <p>
    Four steps, and the button does all of them: take an address from the plan if this sheet has none,
    mint a keypair, run <code>podman run -d --name <%= @sheet.pod_name %> --network none</code>, then
    build a WireGuard interface in the HOST namespace and move it into the pod. The sheet keeps the
    address and the public key; the private key is destroyed with the call.
  </p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>address assigned</th><td><code><%= @sheet.pod_ip.presence || "— none yet (the plan gives the lowest free)" %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>tunnel port</th><td><code><%= @sheet.wg_port.presence || "— none yet" %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>public key</th><td><code><%= @sheet.pubkey.presence || "— none yet" %></code></td></tr>
  </table>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:.4rem 0 1rem">
    History, not state: these record what the last launch did. Neither says the pod is running — that
    question is answered by <a href="<%= pods_path %>">Pods</a>, which asks podman.
  </p>
  <form action="<%= start_sheet_path(@sheet.slug) %>" method="post">
    <input type="hidden" name="authenticity_token" value="<%= form_authenticity_token %>">
    <button class="go" type="submit">start <%= @sheet.pod_name %></button>
    <a class="btn" href="<%= pod_path(@sheet.slug) %>">what the relay says about it</a>
  </form>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0">
    A failure is shown as podman said it. Nothing here records a pod as “failed”, because a record of
    a failure is a claimed current state, and this system does not store those.
  </p>
</div>

<h2>In router.conf right now</h2>
<pre><% Cove::RouterConfig.render([@sheet], Cove::Plan.services, Cove::Plan.network_map).lines.grep(/^(router|peer|service|permit|unresolved) /).each do |line| %><%= line %><% end %></pre>
<p class="muted">Rendered live from this sheet and the service book — read only for this page's sake;
the file itself is written at <a href="<%= router_config_path %>"><code>router.conf</code></a>.</p>
